WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A voice plays one syllable. A face appears to say another.
The soundtrack itself has not changed.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1976, researchers deliberately paired mismatched
speech sounds and lip movements.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
With sound "ba" and visible "ga", some listeners
reported hearing "da"—a third percept.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
But not every listener responds the same way.
A viral clip is not a diagnosis.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
A perception effect does not prove commercial
audio can reprogram a brain.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the paper. See the limits.
Decide what a recording is worth to you.
